      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "The form of WEONA MISS MIKI (9) had tapered off by the end of her last campaign but she was a winner at this circuit and distance earlier in that preparation. Proven when fresh and was readied with a trial win so could make a winning return. JILLIBY ILLUMINATE NZ (10) was good against the boys when returning from a let-up at Penrith last start, working home well to miss narrowly. Better for that and while she draws out she came from a similar barrier to go under by just a head here four back. ROCKIN GEMMA (8) cops a wide draw for her return to Sydney but has been in fine form in Victoria and SA of late, her last-start St Arnaud Cup success her fifth win from her last six outings. POPS JOY (7) has been ticking along okay against the boys so may enjoy getting back to her own sex. PRINCESS OF SAVOY NZ (3) is up in grade but draws well and has finished runner-up in her two outings here since switching from Queensland.",
